[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  The Copper Finch is waking slowly. A barmaid wipes last night's rings from a 
  table. Rain drums against the shutters. At a corner booth, Mara Venn hunches 
  over an open journal, one hand wrapped around a mug gone cold. You say her 
  name. She looks up. A sharp face. Eyes that have spent years reading shadows. 
  "Kael." She gestures to the bench across from her. Closes the journal but 
  keeps a palm flat on its cover. "The Ash Gate?" A pause. She chews the inside 
  of her cheek. "I've been watching it three nights now. The city guard won't 
  go near it — not since Bram's body was found. They call it cursed and leave 
  it to rot." She leans forward. Lowers her voice. "Here's what I know. The 
  lock mechanism is intact — no sign of forced entry. But something's been 
  *using* it. Fresh ash smears on the cobbles every morning. Footprints that 
  start at the gate and go nowhere." She taps the journal. "I sketched them. 
  Barely human. Too long in the toe, too wide at the ball. And the ash — it's 
  not wood ash. It's bone." A beat. Rain drums harder. "Someone's moving bodies 
  through a sealed gate. Or something is. You tell me." 

