[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  The moment hangs — your hand still extended, the compass resting between you. 
  Mara looks at it. Then back at you. A flicker crosses her face — something 
  between a wince and a smile. "Ah. Right." She lets out a breath. "I can't 
  take this." She reaches into her coat, pulls out the compass by its chain, 
  and presses it back into your palm. Her fingers are cold. The brass is warm 
  from being against her ribs. "I was going to. I had a whole speech about 
  sacrifice and trust. But the truth is — " She taps the crescent scar on her 
  gloved hand. "I need you at that gate with me. And you need a compass that 
  actually points *somewhere* when the world goes sideways." She tucks her 
  hands into her coat pockets. "Keep it. I'll take your word instead." The rain 
  softens against the windows. A shutter creaks. The barmaid refills a lantern 
  across the room. Mara tilts her head toward the door. "So. We know the gate's 
  active. We know someone's moving things through it. And we know the Watch 
  won't touch it." She meets your eyes. "What's our first move?" 
