[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  You reach into your pouch. Two gold coins clink against your fingers — worn 
  at the edges, stamped with a mint mark you don't recognize. You place them on 
  the scarred table between you. Mara's eyes drop to the coins. Then back to 
  your face. For a long moment she doesn't move. The tavern hums around you — 
  the barmaid's footsteps, the rain's steady drum, the creak of wet wood. Then 
  she picks them up. One. Two. Slides them into her coat pocket without 
  looking. "Alright." Her voice is quieter now. "That's not nothing. Two gold 
  buys a lot of rope and rations in this city." She leans forward, elbows on 
  the table. "Here's what that buys you. I've got a contact — name's **Sable 
  Tallow**. Runs a chandlery two streets from the gate. She sees everyone who 
  walks past, day or night. And she's been keeping a log of who lingers near 
  the Ash Gate after dark." She taps the table. "We go see her first. Then we 
  scout the gate itself — daylight, just to look. No touching. No testing." She 
  stands. Her chair scrapes the floorboards. "Unless you've got a better idea." 
