[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  You step under the cracked arch of the Ash Gate. The dry ground crunches 
  beneath your boots — ash and grit, not mud. The rain streams past on either 
  side, a curtain of water that frames the gate without touching it. A figure 
  stands in the shadow of the eastern pillar. Young woman. Leather satchel 
  cross-body. Dark hair plastered to her temples by the rain she just walked 
  through. She's watching you with the flat, patient look of someone who's been 
  waiting. You stop. You give your name. You ask the question. She tilts her 
  head. A faint crease forms between her brows — not confusion. Assessment. 
  "Sable Quill." Her voice is dry, a little rough, like she's been shouting 
  over rain all morning. "Courier. And I wasn't waiting for *you* 
  specifically." She pulls a folded, sealed letter from her satchel — cream 
  paper, black wax, no seal impression. "I was waiting for whoever showed up 
  first. Gate's been quiet since Bram died. Then this morning, someone paid me 
  a silver to stand here and hand this to the first person who walked under the 
  arch looking like they meant business." She holds the letter out. Doesn't 
  step closer. Just offers it across the dry gap between you. "Name on it's 
  yours. Kael Windrunner. So either you're him, or you're about to make my job 
  complicated." 

